    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0589" n="575" xml:id="pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.8951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-19">April 19, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>265. For Rubber Development Munro<anchor n="36" xml:id="d443-f1"/> from
                        Truslow.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d443-f2"/> RDC rubber agreement with Bolivia
                    terminates December 31, 1946. No formal agreement has yet been reached on the
                    33⅓ per cent price premium. Agreements with Banco Agrícola also terminate
                    December 31, 1946.</p>
                <p>[Here follow, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi> paragraphs which are
                    the same as telegram 1000, April 19, to Rio de Janeiro, <ref target="#pg704"
                        >page 704</ref>, beginning with second paragraph.]</p>
                <p>A similar proposal is being presented to each other American country
                    participating in rubber program. [Truslow.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d443-f1" n="36" xml:id="d443-f1-content">
                <p>H. H. H. Munro, Special Representative of the Rubber Development Corporation in
                    Bolivia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d443-f2" n="37" xml:id="d443-f2-content">
                <p>Francis A. Truslow, President of the Rubber Development Corporation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
